// Panel: "Daily Energy per Appliance (kWh)"  - Bar chart, Format as: Table.  OWNER: Part 3
// X axis = day (Toronto local date as text), Stacking = Normal, one stacked segment per appliance.
// An hour at an average of X W uses X Wh, so sum(avg_w) / 1000 = kWh per day.
// Today's bar runs slightly high: the hour in progress counts as a full hour.
EnergyHourly
| where $__timeFilter(ts)
| extend day = format_datetime(datetime_utc_to_local(ts, "America/Toronto"), "yyyy-MM-dd")
| summarize kwh = sum(avg_w) / 1000.0 by day, appliance
| evaluate pivot(appliance, sum(kwh))
| order by day asc
